  "title": "EDHOC: Don't use the wrong printf specifier",
  "description": "g_bytes_get_size() returns a gsize, which is almost always a size_t.\n(Subject to a glib bug on some obscure platforms.)\nThere are platforms where a long is 32-bit and a gsize/size_t is\na 64 bit unsigned long long, and compilers that will warn if %ld is used\ninstead of %zu in that case.\n\nPer the comment in !19291, just remove logging the size.",
